{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And it was established.</b> Through the money the field became established as a purchase for Abraham. <b>The field of Ephron.</b> The field extended along the entire face of the city. Here it is called Mamrei — that is Hebron — and above (v. 2) it says Qiryat Arba — that is Hebron. And regarding Jacob it says, ״ויבא יעקב אל יצחק אביו ממרא קרית ארבע היא חברון״ etc., and above regarding Abraham: ״וישב באלוני ממרא אשר בחברון״. This tells you that Mamrei built himself a city facing Hebron, outside it, while Hebron was inside, for the Hittites, and he called it Mamrei by his name, and אלוני ממרא was before it, and מכפלה before the Hittites in a different direction. After the death of Mamrei, the hand of the Anakite whose name was Arba prevailed inside, and he took hold of all of them, and it was called Arba after his name. And when the hand of Israel prevailed and they destroyed the Hittite, they called it Hebron."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:29.578249184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}